<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01243#overallintent_instance> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "meme-id: meme_file_name; hasOverallIntent: overall-intent_id; overall-intent-description: The scene depicts a happy, panting dog looking up at the camera with a grassy background, overlaid with text that reads: 'when your human says \"who's a good girl?\"' and 'and you already know it's you.' The overall intent is to humorously anthropomorphize a dog's perspective, portraying its joyful and self-aware response to being praised by its owner. The meme relies on the relatable and endearing behavior of dogs, using the dog's expressive face and the playful text to create a lighthearted, affectionate moment. There is no toxicity present; the content is innocent, non-abusive, non-cyberbullying, non-harmful, non-hateful, non-misogynous, and not propagandistic. The intent is purely comedic and affectionate, using the visual of the dog's happy expression juxtaposed with the text to evoke a sense of shared human-animal bonding and amusement."@en .
