<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01243#dog_praise_culture> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The meme relies on the common cultural practice of pet owners praising their dogs with phrases like 'good girl' or 'good boy' as a form of positive reinforcement. This is a widely understood interaction in human-animal relationships, especially in Western cultures where dogs are often anthropomorphized and treated as family members. The humor comes from imagining the dog's self-aware, joyful response to this praise, which is a culturally constructed concept not directly visible in the image."@en .
<http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#TargetCommunity> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Target Community"@en .
