<http://w3c.org/memes-ontology/general/01243#dog_training_phrases> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The phrase 'who's a good girl?' is a common verbal cue used by dog owners during training or playtime to reinforce positive behavior. This phrase is culturally specific to pet ownership and training practices, and its use in the meme requires background knowledge of how pet owners interact with their dogs."@en .
